st don't have  the forces but they can mount counter  attacks they can try to take back local  areas they've certainly done it they've  certainly done it somewhere north of  kharkiv they lost hostimel airfield on  the first couple of days but they took  it back and that was not just any old  troops i mean the russians were putting  their best airborne forces into that and  still the ukrainians took it back  they've held it since it looks as if  there's fierce fighting going on there  now so the russians are trying to take  hostimal airfield and that will be  pretty important to the future of kiev  we've been looking at this map for a few  days it does look like they're making  advances around kiev like they're  starting to surround it almost yes and  and a lot of the um uh reports today are  of some fierce fighting on the edges  around the perimeters of kiev to the  west increasingly to the south and of  course these troops that are moving in  from from chernyhiv and sumi um that  again they've they've um uh gone round  those cities they haven't taken them but  they're moving towards kiev the problem  that the russians have is that if you're  invading a country that doesn't want you  there every time you capture somewhere  you've got to leave troops behind to  protect it so the troops at the front of  the push get thinner and thinner so the  push gets harder the further away you  are from your base at some point the  russians will start to run out of troops  strange as it may seem and how many days  do you think it could be before kiev is  totally surrounded well it's hard to  tell they've made very hard work of it  so far but you we have to expect that in  the next let's guess three four days  kiev will probably be surrounded and  then the next phase of this fairly awful  war will on begin to unfold  okay let's look now at another map we  have of the south of the country and we  were talking yesterday about these  ceasefire  areas mario pole home ordinarily to  alm